title: 'pallet-validator-collators: relay-chain validators as system chain collators'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Adds `pallet-validator-collators`, a second session manager for system chains. It stores the
    validator set Asset Hub announces for each era and returns its validators with registered
    keys as collators, next to `pallet-collator-selection` through `UnionSessionManager`, a new
    combinator in `pallet-session` that merges the sets of two session managers. A new set forces
    two session rotations so it takes effect within two blocks.

    Adds `pallet-validator-set-announcer`, which runs on Asset Hub only. It applies the set of
    each era locally and sends it once to each configured system chain through a
    runtime-provided sender, reporting every send with an event. It holds no storage and does
    not retry, since the next era sends the full set again.

    `pallet-staking-async` gains the `OnEraStart` config item, called with the validators of
    each era when it becomes active. Use `()` to keep the previous behaviour.
    storage read and write per era.

    People Westend uses the receiver, and Asset Hub Westend uses both pallets. Asset Hub
    announces every new era to itself and to People. The pallet and call index of People's
    `set_validators` are hard-coded on Asset Hub, and the two runtimes share the validator
    bound.
crates:
- name: pallet-validator-collators
  bump: major
- name: pallet-validator-set-announcer
  bump: major
# `OnEraStart` is a new required config item and `NextEraValidators` is new storage.
- name: pallet-staking-async
  bump: major
# `build_transact_xcm` takes an `OriginKind`.
- name: pallet-staking-async-rc-client
  bump: major
- name: pallet-session
  bump: minor
# Adding the pallets changes the runtimes' public `PalletInstancesInfo` type.
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: major
- name: people-westend-runtime
  bump: major
- name: testnet-parachains-constants
